# Hermes Agent Grounded Search Environment Configuration
#
# Configure Hermes to use the Antigravity Proxy for Gemini Google Search-grounded results.
# This uses Hermes's built-in Tavily search adapter directed at the proxy's /v1/search endpoint.
#
# IMPORTANT:
# - Do NOT point TAVILY_BASE_URL to LiteLLM's port 4000. LLM calls remain on LiteLLM.
# - Do NOT send an existing Tavily subscription key to the proxy.
#   Set TAVILY_API_KEY to the exact value configured for SEARCH_API_KEY in the proxy.
# - If running Hermes on the host: http://127.0.0.1:8000/v1
# - If running Hermes in Docker on the same Compose network: http://antigravity-proxy:8000/v1
# - If running Hermes on a remote host: https://your-proxy-domain.example/v1
#
# WARNING ON EXTRACTION:
# Overriding TAVILY_BASE_URL redirects all Tavily provider calls. If Hermes is configured
# with Tavily for extraction (web.extract_backend: tavily), ensure extraction is configured
# to use a separate backend (e.g., readability, trafilatura, or browser) because this proxy
# only implements search (/v1/search) and does not implement /v1/extract.

TAVILY_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8000/v1
TAVILY_API_KEY=replace-with-the-same-value-as-SEARCH_API_KEY
